	'k3ae246fe' => 'You do not need to bring textbooks, formal documents, or academic transcripts to an open evening. We provide sample syllabus outlines, course schedules, and note-taking paper upon arrival. However, we encourage you to bring an honest assessment of your weekly schedule, including your work commitments and travel time to the Harbourside District. Deciding to prepare for the licence examination requires dedicating at least ten hours per week to independent reading outside the classroom. Having a clear sense of your calendar will help our admissions team advise you whether the evening format or weekend intensive best suits your circumstances.',
	'k3c3640ff' => 'Tuition for our full programmes may be paid in three equal instalments across the academic term. The first instalment is due upon formal registration before the cohort deadline; the second payment falls due at the end of Week 8; and the final payment is due at Week 16. Enrolment deadlines are strictly observed to finalize cohort rosters of 18 students: registration for the Autumn 2026 cohort closes on 7 September 2026, while the Spring 2027 cohort deadline is 5 April 2027. Payments can be arranged directly through Samuel Brandt at the admissions office.',
	'k3d0fa6e6' => '8 weeks. A focused update on recent statute revisions for candidates returning after a career break.',
