	'ka4329567' => 'Evening Licence Course fee',
	'ka5227440' => 'Ines Marlow is the founder and principal of Tochi Academy. A former conveyancer with extensive experience in land registration and ownership transfers, she leads our Week 1 Foundations module on Monday evenings, instilling precise legal habits from the very first lesson. Tomas Reyes leads Contracts &amp; leases on Monday and Wednesday evenings. His background in commercial lease drafting and dispute resolution equips students to analyze covenants, break clauses, and landlord obligations with precision. Priya Natarajan oversees Property law &amp; disclosure on Tuesday evenings. Drawing on years of regulatory compliance work, she guides candidates through disclosure mandates, misrepresentation risks, and statutory seller duties.',
	'ka5c4c1f7' => 'All information collected by Tochi Academy is used exclusively for internal academic and administrative purposes. We use your data to process enrolments, manage instalment payments, provide written instructor evaluations, and communicate essential timetable updates. We never sell, lease, or distribute student records to commercial third parties. Academic records and mock examination assessments are retained securely for the duration of your course and an appropriate statutory retention period following your examination sitting, after which physical papers are shredded and digital records securely archived or deleted in accordance with data protection regulations.',
